Key Stats to Analyze
Runs Scored (Last 3+ Games)

Target batters with 0 runs in their last 3+ games (use MLB game logs or tools like Baseball-Reference).

Plate Appearances (PA)

Filter for players with regular playing time (e.g., 10+ PA in 3 games). Limited opportunities (e.g., pinch-hitting) skew results.

On-Base Percentage (OBP)

Low OBP (< .250) in the streak suggests they’re not reaching base (walks/hits), reducing chances to score.

Slugging Percentage (SLG)

Poor power numbers (SLG < .300) indicate weak contact, making it harder to advance into scoring position.

Batted Ball Data

Check exit velocity and hard-hit rate (via Baseball Savant).

Low exit velocity (< 85 mph) = weak contact.

High hard-hit% but poor results = bad luck (streak may reverse).

Contextual Factors
Team Offense: If the team is slumping (low runs/game), even good hitters may struggle to score.

Lineup Position: Leadoff hitters get more chances to score; bottom-of-order hitters depend on teammates.

Situational Stats:

Team’s performance with RISP (Runners in Scoring Position).

Batter’s performance in high-leverage situations.

Injuries/Workload: Check if the player is nursing an injury or facing fatigue (e.g., playing 15+ straight games).

Example Workflow
Identify Targets: Use FanGraphs to filter batters with 0 runs in 3+ games.

Narrow Down:

Remove part-time players (PA < 10 in 3 games).

Eliminate hitters with strong underlying metrics (e.g., high OBP, hard-hit%).

Team Context: Check if their team ranks bottom 10 in runs scored (e.g., 2023 Oakland Athletics).

Betting/DFS: Use this to fade hitters in prop bets (e.g., "No Runs" props on DraftKings) or avoid in DFS.

Streak-Breaking Indicators
A cold streak may end if:

The batter faces a weak pitcher (high ERA, low strikeout rate).

The team’s lineup improves (e.g., key hitters return from injury).

Underlying metrics (exit velocity, xwOBA) suggest positive regression.

Tools & Sources
MLB Game Logs: Baseball-Reference, ESPN.

Advanced Stats: Baseball Savant (exit velocity, xwOBA).

Team Metrics: FanGraphs Team Stats.

Injury Reports: Rotowire.

Limitations
Runs depend heavily on teammates driving the batter in. A batter with a high OBP but no runs might be unlucky, not slumping.

Small sample sizes (3 games) can be noisy. Look for streaks of 5+ games for stronger signals.

